  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 8 July 2005, that the roof extension, comprising a rear dormer with a 3.3m projection, a height of 2.5m and a width of 5.8m, and a hip to gable alteration measuring a perpendicular depth of 3.75m, a height of 2.7m and a width of 7m, are lawful within the meaning of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\nThe development falls within the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 1, Class B of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the total volume of the proposed development does not exceed 50m3 on the roof, or 70m3 of the original dwellinghouse.\r\n"
